  "findings": [
    "Sign anchor: the particle block of H(k) equals the Bloch matrix rebuilt from the ED one-magnon states (4 x 4 torus, 16 momenta) within 2.7e-14; its complex conjugate, which has the opposite Chern numbers, differs by 2.0. The ED Bloch states alone give C = (+1, -1) by FHS on a 5 x 5 torus. Eigenvalue comparisons (stage 3) could not fix this sign.",
    "dH/dk equals central differences within 6e-10 (relative); the Kubo curvature equals small-plaquette phases of the eigenvectors within 2e-5 (Haldane) and 3e-4 (Kitaev, curvature up to 4, plaquette step 1e-4).",
    "Haldane magnons (J = 1, D = +-0.2, h = 0.3): C = (+1, -1) for D > 0, flipping with D; D = 0 gives zero curvature (1.7e-13).",
    "Kitaev [111] polarized (K = -1, h = 0.5, 1, 2; pairing up to 0.5): FHS C = (+1, -1) on every mesh, Kubo converges to it (h = 2: 0.7745, 0.9700, 0.99956, 0.9999999 at N = 12, 24, 48, 96); the particle bands sum to zero; reversing the field reverses C; the cell gauge gives the same FHS integers.",
    "Triangular Heisenberg (Y-like state at h = 1): Chern numbers 0 within 5e-15 although the pointwise curvature in the full-position gauge reaches 0.81.",
    "Band crossing between mesh points (canted square antiferromagnet, folded bands): the mesh level spacing (>= 4e-3) does not detect it; the FHS link overlap drops to 1e-15 and the Chern numbers are NaN with a warning.",
    "Gap closing between mesh points (Haldane at D = 0, Dirac points): on the 12 x 12 mesh FHS still returns an integer (-1, +1) while the Kubo sum is 0; chern_numbers rejects the pair (NaN with a warning) and the 24 x 24 mesh gives 0 in both. An FHS integer alone is not a Chern number.",
    "Neel state: the two particle bands are degenerate everywhere; curvature and Chern numbers are NaN (band-isolation policy of the issue 260802)."
  ],
